"""In-place ``_foreach_sigmoid_`` implemented with Triton kernels.

Semantics (ATen ``aten::_foreach_sigmoid_(Tensor(a!)[] self) -> ()``):
for every tensor ``t`` of the list, ``t[i] <- 1 / (1 + exp(-t[i]))`` in place,
preserving storage, shape, stride and dtype; the call returns ``None``.

Wrapper strategy (all metadata work only, no host->device staging):
  * contiguous tensors of the same dtype are packed, up to ``_SLOTS`` at a time,
    into ONE Triton launch whose 1-D grid is the concatenation of the
    per-tensor tile counts; each program picks its tensor from the flat
    program id, so a 16-element list costs a single launch instead of 16;
  * a single contiguous tensor uses a plain flat kernel;
  * noncontiguous tensors use a dim-collapsed strided kernel, one launch each.
"""

